### DATA
# Same rule as the sibling projects: no data file goes to GitHub. The workbooks and params.xlsx stay on disk and
# in iCloud, not in the repository. A fresh clone gets the CODE and the DOCUMENTS only and cannot run until the
# workbooks are supplied separately. See README.md.
*.xlsx
*.csv
*.zip
*.pkl
*.npy
*.png

### WRITTEN BY THE STAGES
# Matthias, 2026-10-26: "No figures or other items, which are generated by the code should go into the github
# repository". 01 to 03 draw figures/; 00_parameters.py writes params.xlsx (above) and the parameter reference.
figures/
documentation/claude/PARAMETER_REFERENCE.md
# 02_composition.py writes the draws and summaries of every robot type here, for stock-and-flow.
data/consolidated/
# 04_parts_taken_apart.py writes the draws of robot type 1 taken apart here (their column lists are .txt files).
data/parts_taken_apart/
# 04_stock_and_flow.py writes the draws of the robots, joint sets, battery packs and their elements here (their axes
# in draws.txt).
data/stock_and_flow/
# 02_composition.py writes into staging folders beside its output folders ('<folder>.writing') and moves everything
# into the output folders when every robot type adds up (since 2026-11-13); a stopped run may leave them.
*.writing/
# tools/copy_data_center_draws.py copies RAWCLICDataCenters' 08 draws here (with elements.txt and source.txt); that
# repository is private, so nothing of the copy goes to GitHub.
data/raw/data_center_stock_and_flow/
# 05_combined_stock_and_flow.py writes the draws of the data centres and the robots together here (elements.txt each).
data/combined_stock_and_flow/

